{
  "explanation": "An internal user or compromised asset at IP 10.20.0.99 attempted to exfiltrate sensitive data by downloading a massive customer records export containing personally identifiable information (PII) and financial data, followed by a full system backup archive. The HTTP 200 status codes indicate that both large-scale extraction requests were successful, resulting in the transfer of gigabytes of data using command-line utility tools.",
  "mitre_tactic": "Exfiltration",
  "recommended_actions": [
    "Immediately isolate the source IP 10.20.0.99 from the network to prevent further unauthorized data access.",
    "Revoke active session tokens, credentials, and API access associated with the account utilized during these requests.",
    "Implement rate limiting, strict access controls, and multi-factor authentication on administrative export and backup endpoints."
  ]
}
